  "notes": [
   "The rule is 'Choose a minimum of 18 units': at least 3 units from Humanities and at least 3 units from Fine Arts; the remaining 12 units may come from either category. Each block's minimum is set to 3; the 18-unit total is in total_units.",
   "ART-142, ART-143, ART-145, ART-146, ART-151, ARTH-C1100 and ARTH-C1200 are printed under both Humanities and Fine Arts, so they appear in both blocks; a reviewer should check whether one course may count toward both minimums.",
   "Catalog prints codes with hyphens (e.g., ARAM-120, ARTH-C1100); these were matched to closed-list codes ARAM 120 and ARTHC1100/ARTHC1200 and not flagged as catalog additions. The closed list stores no units for ARTHC1100/ARTHC1200; the catalog prints 3 for each.",
   "General education is described only as 'AS or AA General Education Requirements (see Degree Requirements and Transfer Information section)'; no GE units or degree total are printed.",
   "The program learning outcomes are printed once on the page for this program and recorded as printed (including 'principle elements')."
